#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0425 expect=skipped domain=LB
#note "The gate's SECOND member, pinned separately because it is not redundant: with LBSTRESC absent and LBSTRESU present the rule is gated out, but were --STRESC dropped from Requirements.Variables.All the rule would RUN and read the absent column as all-missing, so not empty(--STRESC) would be false on every row and the scenario would report noViolation instead of skipped. The runner distinguishes the two, so this file is what tells a silent gate erosion from a silent pass. Nothing here is a finding either way: a dataset with no standardised character result has nothing for this rule to check."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset LB class=FINDINGS label="Laboratory Test Results"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col LBSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col LBTESTCD type=Char label="Lab Test or Examination Short Name"
col LBORRES  type=Char label="Result or Finding in Original Units"
col LBSTRESU type=Char label="Standard Units"
col LBORRESU type=Char label="Original Units"
---
S1 | LB | 001 | 1 | GLUC | 7.2 | mmol/L | mg/dL
S1 | LB | 001 | 2 | ALB  | 40  | g/L | g/dL
